      "why": "iterative is the canonical minimum-area CORDIC datapath (single shared barrel-shifter/adder path, no per-stage registers). It is the only family here that can plausibly hit the lowest luts_plus_ffs, which is the selection objective. The throughput constraint (>=1 MSPS) is met as long as Fmax >= (N+3) MHz, which is easily satisfied for the N values that give max_abs_err <= 2^-10. I keep n_iter wide (4..30) because accuracy_bits is a maximisation objective and the Pareto front spans the accuracy-vs-area trade-off; data_width wide (8..28) since W drives both accuracy and area; guards left open so Optuna can find the cheapest guard combination that still meets the error bound."
    },
    {
      "budget_share": 0.45,
      "family": "unrolled_k",
      "ranges": [
        {
          "choices": [
            "trunc",
            "round"
          ],
          "high": 4,
          "low": 0,
          "param": "frac_guard"
        },
        {
          "choices": [
            "trunc",
            "round"
          ],
          "high": 4,
          "low": -2,
          "param": "angle_guard"
        },
        {
          "choices": [

